exit 0

For the pipewire version 0.1.0 of audiod you only need this in /etc/rc.d/rc.local
# Start the audio session manager (needs elogind up first)
if [ -x /etc/rc.d/rc.audiod ]; then
  /etc/rc.d/rc.audiod start
fi

---

For the full Hub version >= 0.2.0 you need ^^ and be sure for these:
activated on /etc/audiod/audiod.conf --> HUB_MODE=yes
add user_name that will be the owner HUB_OWNER=user_name (if empty will be the first who login)
(a name that is not a real user is ignored, check: grep audiod /var/log/messages)

# create the group and add users
groupadd audiohub
gpasswd -a user_name audiohub

#Usage:
audioctl hub status
audioctl hub pair

If you only want the pipewire fix you can disable all above^^

---

removepkg audiod removes everything (needs pkgtools with douninst.sh support,
Slackware 15.0 and later): rc.audiod, /etc/audiod, the rc.local start block,
the takeover edits and the hub guest drop-ins in users' homes
(~/.config/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/89-audiod-hub-no-bluez.conf).
Extra files you put in /etc/audiod and the audiohub group are left and reported.
Upgrades (upgradepkg) do not trigger any of this.
